<title>USA: GM to approve Hughes sale to Raytheon --WSJ.</title>
<headline>GM to approve Hughes sale to Raytheon --WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of General Motors Corp will meet Thursday in New York and is expected to approve the sale of Hughes Electronics' defence operations to Raytheon for about $9.5 billion, The Wall Street Journal reported.</p>
<p>The move would be a loss for competing bidder Northrop Grumman.</p>
<p>GM's approval is expected to be announced late in the afternoon, the newspaper said. It cited sources &quot;close to the situation&quot; who said GM's approval was virtually a foregone conclusion.</p>
<p>All the companies involved declined to comment for the newspaper's report.</p>
</text>
